1
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:06,170
Just like that,
the end of summer quietly slipped away.

2
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:30,250
Time flew by.

3
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:43,600
And we welcomed the inevitable,

4
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,570
highly anticipated day
for Korean high schoolers.

5
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:47,770
Today is the day
of the college entrance exam.

6
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:50,450
The whole country is freezing cold.

7
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:53,020
[10 degrees lower than usual...
The worst cold wave in CSAT history hits]

8
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,800
10 degrees lower than this time
in previous years—

9
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,200
the worst cold wave
in CSAT history has hit.

10
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:58,530
Seoul's morning temperature dropped
to minus 8 degrees.

11
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:00,920
This is for Cha Dohyun.

12
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:04,709
Tell him not to be nervous.

13
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:09,480
All the best.

14
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:14,970
And we,

15
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:19,890
who thought would stay
in that time forever...

16
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:26,480
Hey, the meat is burning. Flip it!

17
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:29,820
Unknowingly got ready to become adults.

18
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:32,630
This time it's your fault.

19
00:01:32,630 --> 00:01:33,870
Come on, cheers! Cheers!

20
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:35,270
Hurry up! Hurry up!

21
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:37,150
Now we are 20 years old.

22
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:39,130
A man's life...

23
00:01:39,259 --> 00:01:41,400
-Starts now!
-Starts now!

24
00:01:43,090 --> 00:01:46,640
Come on! Have more meat.

25
00:01:46,770 --> 00:01:48,340
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

26
00:01:48,470 --> 00:01:49,280
Okay.

27
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:50,640
Sir,

28
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,880
I want a drink.

29
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,050
Go get it yourself.

30
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:55,160
Okay!

31
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:59,350
Hey, what do you want to do
after graduation?

32
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:00,090
Me?

33
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:01,400
I want to be a rapper, sir.

34
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,210
A rapper?

35
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:03,550
That's cool.

36
00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:08,250
You punk.

37
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:14,110
That kind of drink...

38
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:17,170
I should be the one pouring them for you.

39
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:18,770
Come sit down.

40
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:20,690
Thank you.

41
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:25,470
Oh my, you brats

42
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:28,079
have all grown up so quickly.

43
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:30,840
Come on, let me pour you a glass.

44
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:31,520
Thank you!

45
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:32,540
No problem.

46
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:34,320
Here, let me pour you one.

47
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,060
Thank you!

48
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:35,980
All right.

49
00:02:46,010 --> 00:02:48,810
Hey, what are you guys planning to do
in the future?

50
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,240
I want to be a congressman.

51
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:57,660
You're more suited to be the president

52
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,220
than a congressman.

53
00:02:59,570 --> 00:03:02,470
Right? Right?

54
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,920
But someone told me
not to be the president.

55
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:06,990
Who?

56
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,500
Our teacher!

57
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:10,950
He probably doesn't like me.

58
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:12,880
Our teacher...

59
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:14,500
does dislike you.

60
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:16,000
He does.

61
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,650
Damn it. What are you going to do
in the future?

62
00:03:20,970 --> 00:03:22,579
He'll probably going to be a rapper.

63
00:03:22,579 --> 00:03:24,790
Things will work out somehow.

64
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:28,490
He's always so laid-back.

65
00:03:28,690 --> 00:03:30,140
What are you expecting?

66
00:03:30,810 --> 00:03:32,240
As for him...

67
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,690
Forget it.

68
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:36,990
What about you?

69
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:40,680
He just has to take over this place.

70
00:03:41,410 --> 00:03:43,510
Damn, I'm so jealous.

71
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:46,630
I want to be Eunho's underling
instead of the president.

72
00:03:46,630 --> 00:03:48,120
Me too, me too!

73
00:03:48,510 --> 00:03:49,430
Damn it.

74
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:50,760
Me too.

75
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,850
I don't know what to do either.

76
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:54,820
Cheers!

77
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,000
Cheers! Cheers! Cheers!

78
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,700
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

79
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,610
Damn you, Cha Dohyun!

80
00:04:20,149 --> 00:04:22,680
you haven't drunk a drop, right?
Have a glass!

81
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:25,740
Just drink this.

82
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:27,300
No.

83
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:30,820
Then get out.

84
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:32,970
I...

85
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:36,080
I'll corrupt him sooner or later.

86
00:04:37,290 --> 00:04:38,180
You're gonna corrupt him?

87
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:39,840
Hey, Cha Dohyun is already...

88
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,760
Oh man,
closing on a busy day like today...

89
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,030
Are you eating well?

90
00:04:51,230 --> 00:04:52,090
-Yes.
-Yes.

91
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,030
Yes, sir!

92
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:54,830
Wait, why is he so excited?

93
00:04:56,330 --> 00:04:58,210
Why is his face so red?

94
00:04:58,460 --> 00:04:59,060
Oh,

95
00:04:59,970 --> 00:05:02,890
he's just hot from grilling the meat.

96
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:04,370
He did all the grilling?

97
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:06,370
I've been grilling the whole time.

98
00:05:06,370 --> 00:05:07,770
I want another bottle of—

99
00:05:08,090 --> 00:05:09,310
Hey,

100
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:12,170
you guys are still 19.

101
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,890
Not for long, ma'am.

102
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:19,380
In 10 minutes,

103
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,150
we'll be adults.

104
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:23,270
It's almost time.

105
00:05:23,430 --> 00:05:25,040
Wait, wait, wait.

106
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,650
Wow, so many people.

107
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:28,660
Yeah.

108
00:05:27,870 --> 00:05:29,100
[At the scene of Boksingak 2026 Countdown]

109
00:05:29,150 --> 00:05:30,610
Shall we go over there too?

110
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,480
Yeo Eunho.

111
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,320
Let's go.

112
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:41,460
Where to?

113
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,130
Hey, where are you going?

114
00:05:45,130 --> 00:05:47,250
Aren't we counting down together?

115
00:05:47,390 --> 00:05:49,130
Where are you going?

116
00:05:50,590 --> 00:05:51,580
Drink.

117
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:53,120
So annoying.

118
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,420
Hey!

119
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,810
You should at least tell me
where we're going.

120
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:05,810
We've got to hurry up.

121
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,380
Before it's too late.

122
00:06:11,030 --> 00:06:12,550
What are you doing?

123
00:06:25,470 --> 00:06:29,760
Three, two, one.

124
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:43,409
Hello, 20-year-old Yeo Eunho.

125
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,290
You're too impatient.

126
00:07:06,210 --> 00:07:07,520
Impatient?

127
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:10,050
I've held back a long time for this day.

128
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:34,840
Relax.

129
00:08:57,390 --> 00:09:00,510
I told you to relax.

130
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:03,730
You should've given me time to relax.

131
00:09:10,530 --> 00:09:12,130
By the way, are you going out?

132
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:13,830
Get dressed.

133
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:15,380
We're going out.

134
00:09:17,530 --> 00:09:19,020
It's the middle of the night.

135
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:20,260
Where are we going?

136
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:26,430
You'll see when we get there.

137
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:29,070
But I'm tired.

138
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:39,760
Yeo Eunho.

139
00:09:44,230 --> 00:09:45,400
Come here.

140
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:05,670
What's going on? Is the sun not up yet?

141
00:10:13,210 --> 00:10:14,500
Make a wish.

142
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:35,390
I hope I never fight with Yeo Eunho,

143
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:38,020
and we stay happy forever.

144
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:42,280
How many times have I told you
to make a wish in your heart, silly?

145
00:10:42,330 --> 00:10:44,850
It won't come true if you say it out loud.

146
00:10:50,310 --> 00:10:51,430
No.

147
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,760
My wish

148
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,810
will come true.

149
00:11:47,630 --> 00:11:50,300
[Sung Inho]

150
00:11:55,190 --> 00:11:56,900
[Kim Domin]

151
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:19,450
[Summertime]

152
00:12:23,850 --> 00:12:26,830
Why are we
suddenly wearing school uniforms?

153
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:30,590
There aren't many days left
for us to wear school uniforms.

154
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:52,670
Let's go on a date.

155
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:07,020
Thanks.

156
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:17,240
Do you want a sip?

157
00:13:18,110 --> 00:13:19,130
Sure.

158
00:13:23,130 --> 00:13:24,350
Crazy.

159
00:13:37,130 --> 00:13:38,620
It's good.

160
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:40,160
Peace.

161
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,100
So pretty.

162
00:15:20,790 --> 00:15:22,000
Yeah.

163
00:15:27,870 --> 00:15:29,390
Hey, you can't do that—

164
00:15:53,370 --> 00:15:56,220
I would like to offer my
congratulations to all of you

165
00:15:55,090 --> 00:15:56,670
[Congratulations on your graduation]

166
00:15:56,690 --> 00:16:02,160
who are about to enter society.

167
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:05,070
-I sincerely wish...
-Jaewon.

168
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:08,120
-for you to go through every season in peace.
-Let's go to the internet cafe.

169
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:10,440
Didn't the homeroom teacher say
we're celebrating today?

170
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,190
-For your brand new start...
-Why go there?

171
00:16:12,190 --> 00:16:13,240
Said he'd buy us drinks.

172
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:14,570
I'll be cheering you on.

173
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:18,200
Thank you.

174
00:16:18,340 --> 00:16:19,650
Then let's go to the internet cafe
after this.

175
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:20,510
Okay.

176
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:26,270
Finally, please welcome the valedictorian
for the graduation speech.

177
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:29,400
It's Cha Dohyun.

178
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,110
Hello, everyone.

179
00:16:33,370 --> 00:16:37,030
I'm Cha Dohyun, speaking on behalf
of the graduates.

180
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,310
Before we knew it,

181
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:42,510
we've spent 3 summers
and winters here.

182
00:16:43,090 --> 00:16:45,190
Right now, both happy memories

183
00:16:45,330 --> 00:16:48,700
and difficult times come to mind.

184
00:16:49,390 --> 00:16:50,970
In this not-so-short time,

185
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:53,710
we've learned a lot.

186
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,650
Patience and resilience,

187
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,680
friendship and jealousy,

188
00:16:57,830 --> 00:17:01,040
hatred and love, and so on.

189
00:17:01,210 --> 00:17:03,570
That summer of ours
that once felt so unfamiliar

190
00:17:03,570 --> 00:17:06,650
yet passionate which seemed
like it would never end

191
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:09,369
have passed by without you knowing.

192
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:12,069
And we don't know how cold and ruthless

193
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:15,810
the society we're about to enter will be.

194
00:17:16,230 --> 00:17:18,589
Perhaps we will lose our way and wander.

195
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:21,680
Perhaps the day will come
when we drift apart.

196
00:17:22,010 --> 00:17:23,140
But...

197
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:28,760
please don't forget that
after winter comes spring,

198
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:33,350
and summer will eventually arrive again.

199
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,640
Please don't waste time

200
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,180
blaming and regretting the past.

201
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,580
Instead, welcome

202
00:17:39,770 --> 00:17:41,790
the new times ahead with a smile.

203
00:17:42,090 --> 00:17:44,330
Whichever path you take,

204
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:47,940
I sincerely hope your winter
won't be too long.

205
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:52,550
Congratulations on your graduation.

206
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:57,390
One, two, three.

207
00:17:58,650 --> 00:18:00,340
Oh, I blinked.

208
00:18:00,470 --> 00:18:01,130
One more.

209
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:02,450
I'm not going to take anymore.

210
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:04,210
-Take it quickly.
-Hurry up.

211
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,470
Hurry up, do a quick one.

212
00:18:05,470 --> 00:18:06,410
Hurry.

213
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:11,480
One, two, three.

214
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,380
Done.

215
00:18:14,650 --> 00:18:17,500
I heard you got into Hankuk University!

216
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:19,260
Congratulations.

217
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:21,060
Thanks.

218
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,510
Thanks.

219
00:18:22,690 --> 00:18:23,620
This is my son.

220
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:24,730
Is that so?

221
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:25,850
Thank you.

222
00:18:26,570 --> 00:18:27,230
Thanks.

223
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:28,440
Keep in touch.

224
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:30,760
Hey, you guys take a picture.

225
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,540
Yeah.

226
00:18:31,670 --> 00:18:32,410
What for?

227
00:18:32,530 --> 00:18:33,940
Come on, hurry up.

228
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,150
Gosh.

229
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:37,020
Get closer.

230
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:38,730
Look closer. That's right.

231
00:18:38,730 --> 00:18:39,920
Smile!

232
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:41,710
Smile.

233
00:18:57,910 --> 00:18:59,270
I'm leaving right now.

234
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,690
Okay.

235
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,790
You're here.

236
00:19:26,710 --> 00:19:27,780
Sorry.

237
00:19:28,290 --> 00:19:30,000
I wanted to come earlier,

238
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:32,080
but a group of customers came in.

239
00:19:32,530 --> 00:19:34,060
Have you been waiting long?

240
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:35,710
Not really.

241
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,040
Oh,

242
00:19:40,890 --> 00:19:42,970
my mom told me to give this to you.

243
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:49,240
She really didn't have to.

244
00:19:50,170 --> 00:19:51,500
Just take it.

245
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:07,170
Mind if I smoke?

246
00:20:07,610 --> 00:20:08,930
Go ahead.

247
00:20:09,090 --> 00:20:10,910
It's your front door anyway.

248
00:20:24,810 --> 00:20:26,130
Hey, Kwon Yihyun,

249
00:20:26,650 --> 00:20:29,100
the smoke in the club
must be suffocating too.

250
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,360
Aren't you sick of it?

251
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:44,160
How's helping out at the restaurant?

252
00:20:44,650 --> 00:20:45,960
It sucks.

253
00:20:46,330 --> 00:20:49,460
Three minutes in front of the grill
and I'm drenched in sweat.

254
00:20:49,460 --> 00:20:51,520
The aircon doesn't even help either.

255
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,540
I never knew people loved BBQ this much.

256
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,170
I thought it'd be

257
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:10,920
a whole new world after graduation.

258
00:21:13,570 --> 00:21:15,020
Turns out it's not.

259
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:19,390
I actually think
being in school was better.

260
00:21:22,230 --> 00:21:23,220
Oh,

261
00:21:24,050 --> 00:21:26,360
Yoo Wonho started learning welding

262
00:21:26,510 --> 00:21:28,420
through his dad's connection.

263
00:21:29,210 --> 00:21:32,950
Everyone is busy going to college
or finding a job.

264
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:36,000
I'm the only one
who doesn't know what to do.

265
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:42,980
Take your time.

266
00:21:44,450 --> 00:21:45,580
What?

267
00:21:47,990 --> 00:21:51,030
You can be calm
because you have backup.

268
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,570
Kwon Yihyun,

269
00:22:01,420 --> 00:22:03,680
are you going to keep working at the club?

270
00:22:07,270 --> 00:22:08,400
Hard to say.

271
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:12,140
Even as a waiter,

272
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:13,980
it must be dangerous, right?

273
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:20,000
It's fine.

274
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:22,000
Not too bad.

275
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,460
True.

276
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:26,450
You can definitely handle it.

277
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,860
What about Cha Dohyun?

278
00:22:34,690 --> 00:22:35,710
What?

279
00:22:36,570 --> 00:22:38,430
I mean, is he doing well?

280
00:22:53,630 --> 00:22:55,980
We broke up.

281
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:13,180
[Summertime]

282
00:23:13,190 --> 00:23:14,860
Who is he? Someone you know?

283
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:16,310
Yeah,

284
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:18,620
he's my favorite person in the world.

285
